  <div class="section-label">Phase 3 — Weber County Segment</div>
  <h2>1800 North to 4000 South (West Haven)</h2>

  <p>The Phase 3 segment runs from 1800 North in West Point south to 4000 South in West Haven — the portion currently under State Environmental Study.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} Local officials have indicated UDOT is studying an alignment along 5100 West; UDOT has not published a final preferred alternative through the formal State Environmental Study materials.{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes" %} Public ArcGIS working layers reviewed May 23, 2026 show a hybrid concept design and ROW-related technical metadata, but until UDOT publishes formal alignment maps in the Draft State Environmental Study (expected Fall 2026), no final right-of-way boundary has been formally drawn for any parcel in this segment.{% cite "arcgis-sr177-project-layers-may2026" %}{% cite "arcgis-sr177-row-service-may2026" %}</p>

  <p>UDOT's stated standard footprint is <strong>250 feet</strong>, designed to accommodate four travel lanes separated by a median and flanked by multi-use trail corridors.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %} Applied to a 5100 West centerline, that footprint would extend 125 feet to each side of the road. Properties within roughly 500 feet of the eventual centerline will be evaluated for noise impacts; properties within the 250-foot right-of-way boundary would be subject to acquisition once the project is funded.</p>

