  <div class="callout warning">
    <p><strong>Current status:</strong> No final preferred alignment has been officially selected as of May 23, 2026. The State Environmental Study is in the Alternatives Development and Evaluation phase. Public working GIS includes ROW-related technical layers, but property impacts will not be formally determinable until UDOT publishes the Draft State Environmental Study with formal right-of-way boundaries.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label">Phase 4 — Long-Range Segment</div>
  <h2>4000 South to Box Elder County Line</h2>

  <p>The segment south of 4000 South extending toward the Box Elder County line is in the long-range planning window under the Wasatch Front Regional Council 2023–2050 Regional Transportation Plan (2043–2050 phase).{% cite "wfrc-rtp-2023-2050" %} No State Environmental Study has been initiated for this segment, and no alignment, footprint, or design has been determined. Phase 4 planning will begin in a future study cycle; the source record does not support further specificity.</p>

  <div class="section-label">Residential &amp; Agricultural Displacement Data</div>
  <h2>Davis County Phase 2 — Closest Available Analog</h2>

  <p>No final Weber County State Environmental Study parcel-level impact data has been published. Public working GIS should not be treated as an acquisition list or final impact determination. The Phase 2 Davis County re-evaluation (2024–2025){% cite "udot-wdc-phase2-noise" %} provides the best available historical analog: design refinements between the 2017 Environmental Impact Statement and the updated study expanded the project footprint, increasing impacts across all resource categories.</p>

